Optimal Solution - Simulates integer increment by handling carry propagation from right to left.
                   Add from the end, stop early if no carry remains; only allocate a new array when all digits are 9.

class Solution {
    public int[] plusOne(int[] digits) {
        // Length of the digits array
        int n = digits.length;
        // Start from the last digit
        int i = n - 1;
        // Traverse digits from right to left
        while (i >= 0) {
            // If current digit is less than 9, just increment and return
            if (digits[i] < 9) {
                digits[i]++;
                return digits;
            }
            // If digit is 9, it becomes 0 due to carry
            digits[i] = 0;
            i--;
        }
        // If all digits were 9, we need an extra digit
        int[] res = new int[n + 1];
        res[0] = 1; // e.g., 999 + 1 = 1000
        return res;
    }
}

Time Complexity :- O(n).
Space Complexity :- O(n).
